  "description": {
    "format": "nuke_help_html",
    "plain_text": "F_DeFlicker2 4.6v4.539224 F_DeFlicker2 is used to get rid of two types of flicker from a shot, in-scene and archive. In-Scene flicker is localised, for example from an unsynchronised fluorescent light, and dependent on the geometry of the scene. Archive flicker is smoothly, spatially varying flicker, such as that from an old black and white film. See also F_DeFlicker1 in the full Furnace suite. Help->Documentation contains a more detailed description of this plug-in. Copyright 2026 The Foundry all rights reserved.",
    "source": "nuke.Node.help()",
    "text": "F_DeFlicker2 4.6v4.539224\n\nF_DeFlicker2 is used to get rid of two types of flicker from a shot, in-scene and archive. In-Scene flicker is localised, for example from an unsynchronised fluorescent light, and dependent on the geometry of the scene.\n\nArchive flicker is smoothly, spatially varying flicker, such as that from an old black and white film.\n\nSee also F_DeFlicker1 in the full Furnace suite.\n\nHelp->Documentation contains a more detailed description of this plug-in.\n\nCopyright 2026 The Foundry all rights reserved."
  },
